Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Stained Glass OS: Qt 6 programs draw their Qt Quick scenes with OpenGL, not
; Direct3D 11. Qt WebEngine hands each web frame to Qt Quick as a shared
; Direct3D 11 texture, and our Direct3D 11 (DXVK on Wine's Vulkan) cannot
; share textures (no VK_KHR_external_memory_win32), so every Qt 6 WebEngine
; window stayed blank white -- GOG GALAXY's (qa4, qa5), calibre's viewer.
; With OpenGL the frames need no sharing. Qt 5 draws with OpenGL already and
; reads this only with QSG_RHI set. A machine environment variable, as on
; Windows: Settings > Environment Variables shows it; a program's own
; Compatibility settings (Environment) can set it otherwise.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\System\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager\Environment]
"QSG_RHI_BACKEND"="opengl"
